  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 352 AM EDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nMonday, behind the cold front, surface high pressure along with \nupper ridging reach the CWA, bringing drier conditions to the \nregion, but as the center of the high passes to our north, WAA \nreturns for Tuesday. This will lift highs back into the low to mid \n90s for the middle of next week.  \n\nThrough at least Wednesday as the upper ridge becomes more \npositively tilted, the center of the upper high will sit centered \nnear the Tennessee Valley. This has pushed precipitation chances from \na front riding over the ridge farther north, trending our \nprecipitation chances lower through at least midweek, but by \nThursday or Friday, as the upper high drifts west of the \nMississippi, northwest flow could help push a cold front through the \nLower Ohio Valley. This will provide additional precipitation \nchances later in the week for southern Indiana and central Kentucky. \nIt will also bring a return of falling temperatures with highs only \nreaching into the 80s by the weekend.",
